00:06:42.640 --> 00:06:45.270
So we're excited about
all the opportunities

00:06:45.270 --> 00:06:46.980
between Google Cloud and Unity.

00:06:46.980 --> 00:06:48.510
MARK MANDEL: For
those people who

00:06:48.510 --> 00:06:50.400
may not be familiar
with Unity, Brett,

00:06:50.400 --> 00:06:52.410
do you want to tell us a
little bit about what Unity is?

00:06:52.410 --> 00:06:54.160
BRETT BIBBY: Well, the
easiest description

00:06:54.160 --> 00:06:56.190
is Unity is the world's
leading game engine.

00:06:56.190 --> 00:06:58.710
But it's really a platform
for building real time

00:06:58.710 --> 00:07:03.900
interactive experiences that
run on more than 30 platforms.

00:07:03.900 --> 00:07:05.820
Its success, though,
I think is the key,

00:07:05.820 --> 00:07:07.040
like why does it exist?

00:07:07.040 --> 00:07:09.690
And it's just Unity
allows rapid development

00:07:09.690 --> 00:07:12.780
using an extensible editor and
gets you onto the platforms

00:07:12.780 --> 00:07:14.720
that you need to be successful.

00:07:14.720 --> 00:07:16.290
And that's really
the secret sauce.

00:07:16.290 --> 00:07:17.970
Been that way for a decade.

00:07:17.970 --> 00:07:22.650
And with the diversity and
explosion in devices and OSes

00:07:22.650 --> 00:07:25.620
and the complicated
things around that,

00:07:25.620 --> 00:07:27.980
it just turns out that it's
a useful way to do that.

00:07:27.980 --> 00:07:30.107
And we help make people
be successful with that.

00:07:30.107 --> 00:07:32.190
MELANIE WARRICK: So, Mark,
you alluded to the fact

00:07:32.190 --> 00:07:33.130
that there was an announcement.

00:07:33.130 --> 00:07:34.236
